  {
    "id": "ex39-tab",
    "type": "tab",
    "label": "SITL 39 AP reposition CHANGE_MODE",
    "disabled": false,
    "info": "Throwaway probe (delete when §14 records the answer). Fills the empty cell example 27 left: 27 measured ArduCopter with the vehicle ALREADY in GUIDED and CHANGE_MODE OFF. This run is the inverse — vehicle deliberately NOT in GUIDED, CHANGE_MODE ON.",
    "env": []
  },
  {
    "id": "ex39-comment",
    "type": "comment",
    "z": "ex39-tab",
    "name": "AP reposition from LOITER with CHANGE_MODE set",
    "info": "Flow: Arm -> Takeoff 10 m (both in GUIDED, which AP needs for NAV_TAKEOFF) -> settle -> Set Mode LOITER (custom_mode 5) -> settle -> Move reposition with changeMode TRUE.\n\nWHY: examples 27 and 30 did not run the same experiment. 27 was AP pre-switched to GUIDED with the flag OFF; 30 was PX4 with no mode arrangement and the flag ON. Each stack was tested only in the configuration expected to work for it, so 'both firmwares answer the same way' rests on two different experiments. This probe closes the AP half.\n\nSOURCE HYPOTHESIS (ArduCopter GCS_MAVLink_Copter.cpp, handle_command_int_do_reposition):\n\n  const bool change_modes = ((int32_t)packet.param2 & MAV_DO_REPOSITION_FLAGS_CHANGE_MODE) == ...;\n  if (!copter.flightmode->in_guided_mode() && !change_modes) {\n      return MAV_RESULT_DENIED;\n  }\n  ... set_destination ... then set_mode(GUIDED) if not already, MAV_RESULT_FAILED if that fails\n\nSo the prediction is ACCEPTED, with the vehicle switching itself out of LOITER into GUIDED. A DENIED or FAILED is an equally publishable measurement and PASSES this run — what fails is a send that never reached the wire.\n\nDO NOT assert a resulting heading here. The same handler calls set_destination(loc, false, 0, false, 0) — use_yaw false, yaw 0 — so ArduCopter ignores param4 entirely for DO_REPOSITION. Example 27's 'yaw 90 turns east' expectation cannot hold on Copter (ArduPlane does read param4, for loiter direction). Yaw is left blank here so the run does not restate a claim the firmware cannot honour.\n\nWHAT THE RIG SHOULD RECORD:\n1. mode status — did the LOITER change ACK? (if it did not, the probe's precondition never held and the reposition result means nothing)\n2. reposition status — result, detail, resultCode, retries\n3. Whether the vehicle ended up in GUIDED afterwards (HEARTBEAT custom_mode 4)"
  },
